+// LOCAL PATCH - MCLA (0520): gpu_timing_ops.
+REXCVAR_DEFINE_BOOL(gpu_timing_ops, false, "GPU/Timing",
+                    "With gpu_timing 1: also time the GPU work of each emulation operation per render phase, read at "
+                    "the start of each frame. Each operation is bracketed by two timestamps (begin before its first "
+                    "command, end after its last): resolves (the whole of IssueCopy, with the dual write and the "
+                    "memory write; resolve_dw = the ones that also wrote a texture), texture loads (dispatches and "
+                    "barriers), EDRAM transfers (xfer) and resolve clears (clear), shared memory uploads, and "
+                    "barrier batches outside those (an operation inside another counts for the outer one only, "
+                    "except that the transfers and resolve clears inside a resolve are carved out of it: resolve "
+                    "is then the rest of IssueCopy). "
+                    "Adds the 'ops' log line and, if on when the CSV starts, the <group>_<class>_us / _n columns of "
+                    "gpu_timing_csv. A timestamp is an end-of-pipe point: every bracket makes the GPU drain the work "
+                    "before it (and the begin timestamp may be written before earlier draws have finished, so a "
+                    "bracket can include some of that drain), which costs overlap: the frame gets slower, the phase "
+                    "times are no longer the normal ones, and many brackets (barriers) cost the most. Each frame "
+                    "has room for 4096 timestamps (barrier brackets stop at 3/4 of it), the brackets after that "
+                    "are counted as overflow")
+    .lifecycle(rex::cvar::Lifecycle::kHotReload);
+
